.vercel

# Local environment. Only the .example templates are committed — a real .env
# holds secrets, and the root one was unprotected until now.
#
# The negation matters: .env.* alone would swallow .env.example too, leaving
# newcomers with no template and no hint that one ever existed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Conflict copies a file-sync service drops into the tree on its own. The Go
# ones redeclare their package's types and break the build; it has also renamed
# node_modules binaries out from under the bundler.
* [0-9].*
